  "solution": {
    "text": "Let two particular boys as one boy, we have only four boys which can be seated at a round table in <math><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;ways.<br />The two boys together can be arranged in <math><mn>2</mn></math> ways.<br />So, boys can be seated in <math><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></math> ways.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0074_fa31cf18963c.png\" style=\"width:1.66667in;height:1.67986in\" /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are together. Now <math><mn>4</mn></math> girls can be seated at four places (marked <math><mo>×</mo></math>) in <math><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></math> ways.<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> Required number of ways <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>288</mn></math> ways"
  }
}